let expanded = false;
```

And in CSS:
```css
.msg.assistant .msg-collapse-header { ... }
.msg.assistant .msg-collapse-toggle { ... }
.msg.assistant .msg-collapse-label { ... }
.msg.assistant .msg-collapse-body { ... }
.msg.assistant .msg-collapse-body.hidden { ... }
```

So the web UI has assistant messages wrapped in a collapsible container. The user is saying:
1. The model's reply is completely folded (collapsed) - they can't see it
2. They want it collapsible, but when expanded, they should see the reply, tool calls, etc.
3. The final summary/response should NOT be inside the collapsed area

This is about the WEB UI, not the TUI! Let me look at the web main.ts to understand the full context.

